=== 06:31 UTC 2026-09-21 PRE-REGISTRATION -- SERVED LOOP ON LUNA, SAMPLE 7: does a finished plan's answer-now line cause the stops in words? One build that draws lots inside the run, one run at a time, at most four ===

WHY THIS SAMPLE. The 05:10 block found that on the build with ADR-0205, 21 of 28 refused stops answered one of the 43
requests that carried a finished plan's answer-now line, and that it could not tell the line from the moment: the
line rides exactly when a plan has just finished, which is also when a model is most likely to feel done. One more
free re-read of the same three runs, with the reader committed beside this block, puts a number on the moment. Call
an EPISODE one stretch, inside one turn, during which a finished plan stays on the board. Sample 6 holds 29 of them
and EVERY ONE ended in a stop the model made in words: C 5 of 5, T 11 of 11, T2 13 of 13. In 19 of the 29 the stop
came on the first request that named the finished plan. 23 of the 29 lay in a turn where a refused stop had already
delivered a skill. So with the line sent, the share that stops is at its ceiling. What no run has measured is the
same moment WITHOUT the line.

WHAT CHANGED SINCE THE 05:10 BLOCK, which said the next step was a third veto-door registration forked at this
position, with the served sample after it. That route was sized and not taken (PR #589, bench/README.md). A fork that
deep was estimated at about $7 for one reading, three times registration 2. And the bench world's own loop skill asks
for a closing report in words at the end of every cycle, so at that fork an arm that silences the line could not
show it. The served loop is the place the question is about. Drawing lots INSIDE a run also removes the thing that
limited sample 6 to one run per arm: each run holds both treatments at the same kind of moment, and the unit becomes
a pair of finished plans instead of a run.

THE BUILD. K is main 87cd349 plus bench/served_builds/k.patch: 136 lines, one file (src/zakcode/agent/loop.py),
sha256 prefix 5eae8391d012ca5d, src tree 35fdb8df324e (main's is 71a5802643fa). K IS A MEASUREMENT BUILD AND IS NEVER
MERGED: it draws lots, and a product does one thing. It carries the scope rule of arm L (veto_door_arms/l.patch, PR
#589): once an honoured refusal has named a skill re-entry in a turn, the hook and not the plan decides when that turn
may end. Under L every plan that finishes later in that turn would have its answer-now line kept silent. K does that
to a RANDOM HALF of them:
  - each such plan gets ONE draw, made while its first request is built and held for as long as that plan stays
    finished; the reminder and the per-request trace label read the same predicate, so they cannot disagree;
  - draws come in PAIRS: the first plan of a pair by a fair coin (the OS's random source, no seed), the second the
    other side. Pairs are numbered from 1 in each turn and never span two turns;
  - each draw is written to the trace (pair, slot, side) BEFORE the usage event of the request it governs;
  - a plan that finishes BEFORE any refusal in its turn is outside the scope, on L and on K alike: it is sent its
    line and draws nothing.
Everything else is main: ADR-0204's rails on every request, ADR-0205 (a plan whose stop was refused stays silent, on
both sides alike), and ADR-0206, of which this is the first served run and about which nothing is read here.

PROVEN OFFLINE AND FREE, before this block.
  The build  served_coin_build_proof.py drives the real Agent with the real shell Stop hook and a scripted model in
             the veto-door world, with the coin forced each way. 20 checks pass in K's built tree: nothing is drawn
             before the refusal; three plans finished after it draw pair 1 slot 1, pair 1 slot 2, pair 2 slot 1; the
             second slot is the other side; each side is on the WIRE and in the trace label, also one request later
             for a plan that lingers; a new turn starts at pair 1 owing nothing. Run on main's own source 13 of the
             20 fail: the proof cannot pass without the build. Seven mutants of K (no reset at a turn's start, a draw
             on every request, the second slot the same side, the scope ignored, a draw never released, always sent,
             the coin ignored) each fail a named check, each shown to import its own copy of the tree.
  The reader served_coin.py, 48 known-answer checks on synthetic traces. 26 mutants each fail a named check and the
             unchanged copy passes (served_coin_mutants.py, committed, runs both proofs). On sample 6's worlds it
             gives the 29 of 29 above and finds no draw, as it must.
  The gate   G3 below passed inside the sandbox in the right shape and FAILED in three wrong ones: no build selected
             (the editable install, which is main), a build path that names nothing, and main's real tree asked as K.

THE ASSEMBLY is sample 6's, rebuilt by the same script from the same seed: seed 2.12.76 (sha256 prefix
71c88a26f3b953c0), the provisioning step and its assertions, the same sandbox, ceremony, caps (2400 s run, 350 s
reserve, 2520 s supervisor wall clock, $6.00 supervisor budget per run), trace directory and claim-endpoint patch
(sha256 prefix 74b5eca7c44d0189); no reasoning_effort configured, so the product's forced none applies (ADR-0200).
run_served.sh, progress.py and served.env are compared by hash with the sample-5 control world's by the launcher. The
build is selected inside the sandbox by PYTHONPATH=/srv/zc-builds/K/src, a git worktree one commit on main.
  World 1: zc-served7r1-1ff2a8d6, built and never run. A later world is built by the same script only when its run
  is licensed (THE SEQUENCE, below).

THE GATES, asserted by the launcher before any spend. A failure means the run is NOT READ.
  G1  K's worktree is one commit on 87cd349 and clean; its src tree hash is the registered one; its diff from main
      is BYTE FOR BYTE origin/main's bench/served_builds/k.patch, and it changes nothing outside src/.
  G2  the world is provisioned and unrun: initialised, agent state IDLE, 0 session files, no serve.log, starting queue
      7234 bytes, meta tier uninitialised, the patched claim endpoint, no reasoning_effort in served.env, the three
      kit files identical to the control's, no leaked mount.
  G3  INSIDE the sandbox, under the run's own environment: zakcode imports from K's tree; the draw predicate, the
      draw note and the scope note are in its source; a fresh loop holds an OS-seeded coin, no pair open and no side
      owed; ADR-0204 and ADR-0205 are present; the five luna categories send reasoning_effort none WITH tools and no
      field without, and classify sends none either way; the idle-window stop is unset.
  G4  this block is on origin/main, and the reader in the checkout that will read the run is origin/main's, byte for
      byte. The launcher fetches and checks both, draining its pipes (the 03:18Z lesson of sample 6).
  G5  the live Mind's daemon on this box answers health before and after each run, and no mount leaked.
  After the run, from the artifacts:
  G6  the run's first progress line names K's tree as the zakcode source, and the run wrote its last line.
  G7  every usage event carries rails; the trace holds at least one scope note and one draw; and NO DRAW IS
      CONTRADICTED. A draw is contradicted if it came up silent and the line was then sent; if it came up sent and
      the episode's first unrested request did not carry the line; if the reader places it before any refused stop
      had delivered a skill in its turn (the reader and the build then disagree about the scope); or if a pair's
      draws are not slot 1 then slot 2 on opposite sides. A contradicted run is not repaired or trimmed: it is left
      out whole.

WHAT IS READ, all of it from the per-turn traces, labels and counts only.
  An episode opens at the first request that names a finished plan (line sent or kept silent), or at a draw, and
  closes at the first request that names an open plan or none. A rested request inside it belongs to it. It STOPPED
  IN WORDS if any of its requests was answered by a stop the model made itself: words that a turn-end hook refused,
  or words that ended the turn. A stop the stuck ladder made after tool calls is counted apart and is not one.
  An episode counts under the side it DREW. The unit is a COMPLETE PAIR: the two episodes of one pair number in one
  turn, one drawn sent and one drawn silent. A draw whose partner never came (the turn or the run ended first) is
  reported and not used.
  Over the complete pairs of every run that is read: s is the share of SENT episodes that stopped in words, h the
  share of SILENT ones, and p the exact two-sided sign test over the pairs whose two episodes differ.

THE READING RULE, over every outcome, fixed before launch and coded in served_coin.py (RULE, verdict, reading).
  RUN NOT READ        a gate fails, the trace is refused, a draw is contradicted, or the run holds fewer than 3
                      complete pairs. None of its pairs is used. It still counts as one of the four runs.
  NOT MEASURED        the runs read hold fewer than 12 complete pairs once the sequence below has ended. The numbers
                      are reported as a description and nothing is concluded.
  HARM                h - s >= 20 points and p < 0.05, and that size holds with any ONE pair left out. It is read
                      even where s is under the floor: silence can make things worse where there is little to gain.
  NOT DISCRIMINATING  s < 30% (and not HARM). With the line sent the model seldom stopped, so there is nothing for
                      silence to reduce. It would also contradict sample 6, where 23 of 23 such episodes stopped.
  GAIN                h <= s / 2, and s - h >= 20 points, and p < 0.05, all holding with any ONE pair left out (the
                      size is re-taken without the pair; the p is not, because losing a pair always costs power and
                      says nothing about whether that pair carried the result).
  FLAT                s and h are nearer than 20 points.
  MIXED               anything else, including a GAIN or a HARM that one pair can undo, which is then named with the
                      pairs it rests on. Reported with its direction.
  Thresholds met exactly are met; p must be UNDER 0.05. Every one of the 455 ways 12 pairs can fall lands in exactly
  one branch (enumerated in the selftest). Rule E stands: an outcome nobody named is reported as measured and never
  upgraded.

THE SEQUENCE. Runs are launched ONE AT A TIME, each in a fresh world. After a run, its gates and its PAIR COUNT are
taken, and nothing else: the after-run script prints gates, draw counts and contradictions, writes the full reading
to a file, and prints no stopped-or-not figure for either side. The next run is launched if and only if the runs read
so far hold fewer than 12 complete pairs and fewer than 4 runs have been launched. That rule looks at a count the
treatment cannot favour, so it cannot steer the result. The reading is taken ONCE, after the last run, over every
run read. Sample 6's two runs of this kind would have given 4 and 6 complete pairs, so 2 to 3 runs are expected.

WHAT EACH READING WOULD CHANGE.
  GAIN   The line causes stops in words at this position, for this model in this loop. Arm L becomes a product
         change on main: one behaviour, no flag and no draw, with tests and its own mutation proof (ADR-0207).
         Whether that then changes a WHOLE run (refused stops, the time spent getting back to work, laps closed)
         is a separate registration with a concurrent control; nothing here pre-judges it.
  FLAT   The stops at this position are the model's own and the line is not what makes them. L does not ship. The
         next work goes to what a refused stop COSTS rather than how often one happens: the 05:10 block's 21.7% and
         36.2% of a run spent getting back to work.
  HARM   L does not ship, and the result is recorded against L's argument.
  MIXED  with h < s: one more batch under this same rule (fresh worlds, at most four runs, 12 pairs), read ALONE and
         not pooled. That is a second look, and it is priced here: the chance that one of two looks reads a false
         GAIN is at most the sum of the two, about 0.1. A second MIXED ends the question at this price and L does
         not ship on this evidence. With h >= s: L does not ship and nothing further is licensed.
  NOT DISCRIMINATING  No further run. What differs from sample 6's T build is then named, and it is short: K's patch,
         and ADR-0206, the one commit between c22b46f and 87cd349 that touches src.
  NOT MEASURED        No further run is licensed by this registration.

ESTIMATES, recorded before launch so that each can be scored.
  a launched run is read                                   80%
  complete pairs in a run that is read                     4 to 6 (median 5)
  runs launched                                            2: 20%   3: 55%   4: 25%
  12 pairs are reached within 4 runs                       90%
  s, the sent side                                         90%   (I would be surprised under 75%)
  h, the silent side                                       45%   I do not know this; 15% to 75% would not surprise me.
                                                                 Nobody has run this model at this moment without
                                                                 the line. Against a low h: the loop skill's text
                                                                 has just arrived and a finished checklist invites
                                                                 a summary with or without a reminder.
  the reading                                              GAIN 40%, MIXED 30%, FLAT 15%, NOT MEASURED 8%,
                                                           NOT DISCRIMINATING 5%, HARM 2%
  a silent episode that does not stop lasts at most 3 requests before the model plans again      60%

SECONDARY MEASURES, reported and deciding nothing. Per side: on which request of its episode each stop came; how
many requests each episode lasted; what answered each episode's first request. Per run: episodes outside the scope
(expected: sent, and stopped); finished plans inside the scope that were never drawn (a plan that was already the
refused one when it first met a request); draws left unpaired; refused stops and what each answered, the loop's own
re-entries, the share of the run spent getting back to work, and which laps closed and how (served_stops.py); turns
ended veto_stall and idle seconds (served_rests.py; sample 6's T and T2 had none); calls, cost, cached share; goals
completed.

WHAT THIS CANNOT SETTLE, whatever it reads. Anything about a model other than gpt-5.6-luna at effort none, or a loop
other than this framework's at this seed. The episodes of a run share one conversation. The sign test is exact all
the same under the hypothesis it tests, that the line changes nothing anywhere, because the coin and not the
conversation puts each plan on its side; but h and s as ESTIMATES carry whatever an earlier episode of the same run
left behind (a stop that was refused, a skill body delivered), met in random order. K IS NOT L: under L every plan in
scope would be silent, and K's runs are half and half, so no whole-run figure of K's says what L's would be. Whether
fewer stops in words closes more goals. Why a model stops on a request that carried no line.

SPEND. The supervisor bounds each run at $6.00 and 2520 s, as in every earlier sample. Expected $1.6 to $1.9 a run
(sample 6's T cost $1.63 and T2 $1.88), so about $3.3 to $7.6 for two to four runs. The bound is not lowered: a
budget stop would end a run for a reason that is neither side's doing. Campaign spend so far: about $14.23. No other
model call is made while a run is in flight, and K's worktree is not touched until the sample is read.

